{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/questions.json docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part1.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/questions.json docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part1.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"question\": \"v1\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"What total amount in USD of NVIDIA’s credit-support commitments and minimum-revenue guarantees or backstops to AI labs and cloud partners, including the support for the additional lab’s nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity, will be disclosed in NVIDIA’s FY2027 Form 10-K and related quantified disclosures by the annual report’s publication?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The disclosed amount of guarantees, credit-support commitments and revenue backstops NVIDIA has extended to AI labs and cloud partners (including the credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity for one additional AI lab), versus the equity investments it has made, at NVIDIA's next annual report.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-04-01\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"below 10,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 25,000,000,000 USD to below 50,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 50,000,000,000 USD to below 100,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"100,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v2\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"How much in purchase obligations and supply commitments will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K, as reported in the purchase obligations and contractual commitments disclosures and related notes?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The amount of purchase obligations/supply commitments NVIDIA reports in its contractual obligations and purchase commitment disclosures in the Form 10-K, versus the prior year, given the analyst report that NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-04-01\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"below 50,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 50,000,000,000 USD to below 100,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 100,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 150,000,000,000 USD to below 200,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"200,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v3\",\n  \"about\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n  \"kind\": \"theme\",\n  \"asks\": \"By January 31, 2027, will U.S. authorities authorize Nvidia to sell Blackwell-generation AI chips to China and will Chinese authorities permit those shipments?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether U.S. authorities extend export approval beyond the older H200 to Nvidia's current Blackwell-generation chips for approved Chinese customers, and whether Chinese authorities stop restricting Nvidia chip shipments, so that China data-center revenue can resume; the item reports H200 shipments are already U.S.-permitted while Chinese authorities still restrict them.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"By January 31, 2027, U.S. authorities have authorized sales of Nvidia Blackwell-generation AI chips to China and Chinese authorities permit those shipments.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 23, 2026, U.S. export-control authorities formally prohibit Blackwell exports to China, or Chinese authorities formally prohibit Nvidia Blackwell shipments, with the prohibition remaining in force through January 31, 2027. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-23 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v4\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"Will NVIDIA disclose in its quarterly results or FY2027 Form 10-K that Vera Rubin made volume customer shipments with first revenue recognition by the end of FY2027 (January 31, 2027)?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether Vera Rubin moves from full production to volume customer shipments and first revenue recognition within NVIDIA's fiscal 2027, as shown in the company's quarterly results and Form 10-K.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"NVIDIA's quarterly results or FY2027 Form 10-K show that Vera Rubin made volume customer shipments with first revenue recognition by January 31, 2027.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 23, 2026, NVIDIA formally cancels or abandons the Vera Rubin platform before it makes volume customer shipments. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-23 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v5\",\n  \"about\": \"ai-capex\",\n  \"kind\": \"theme\",\n  \"asks\": \"How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data centers in calendar 2026, as shown by their Q4/full-year 2026 earnings and capex disclosures?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The big five AI hyperscalers' combined calendar-2026 data center capital expenditure, compared with the nearly $800 billion the article says they will spend this year.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-03-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 775,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 775,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"from 775,000,000,000 USD to below 825,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 775,000,000,000 USD to below 825,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"the big five AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data centers this year\\\")\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"from 825,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 825,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"900,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"900,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v6\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"Will NVIDIA complete (close) its agreed acquisition of Hugging Face, as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings, by March 24, 2028?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether the agreed ~$12.9 billion Hugging Face acquisition is signed and closed (completed) as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings, versus being repriced, delayed past the check date or terminated.\",\n  \"due\": \"2028-03-24\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"NVIDIA completes the Hugging Face acquisition by March 24, 2028, as evidenced by NVIDIA's filings or a completion announcement.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After 2026-09-25, NVIDIA or Hugging Face formally terminates or withdraws the acquisition agreement before it is completed. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-25 and stands on 2028-03-24, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-03-24.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v7\",\n  \"about\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n  \"kind\": \"theme\",\n  \"asks\": \"Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology (MIIT) formally approve purchases of Nvidia's RTX Pro 5500 by Alibaba, ByteDance, or other Chinese firms by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether MIIT moves from signaling intent and collecting purchase plans to actually approving Alibaba's, ByteDance's and other Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500 (versus blocking, delaying or capping quantities), so that Nvidia can ship the product into China and book related revenue.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"MIIT formally approves by January 31, 2027, a purchase of RTX Pro 5500 chips by Alibaba, ByteDance, or another Chinese firm.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 27, 2026, MIIT formally rejects all RTX Pro 5500 purchase plans from Alibaba, ByteDance, and other Chinese firms, or formally prohibits those firms from purchasing the chips. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-27 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n][\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e1\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA released Isaac ROS 5.0, a collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on ROS, at the ROSCon conference in Toronto; the release is free and open source, adds support for ROS Lyrical and Ubuntu 24.04, and scales across compute from Jetson Orin Nano to Jetson Thor.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA Isaac ROS 5.0 — a collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on ROS, released today at the ROSCon conference in Toronto, Canada — helps humans and AI agents build robots together. … Isaac ROS 5.0 introduces support for ROS Lyrical and Ubuntu 24.04, giving developers a path to adopt the latest ROS platform while continuing to accelerate demanding robotics workloads with NVIDIA accelerated computing. … Isaac ROS 5.0 supports scalable compute, from entry-level NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano to high-performance Jetson Thor devices, giving developers a path from development to deployment as robotics workloads become increasingly sophisticated. … Available now, Isaac ROS 5.0 is free and open source.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e2\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"RealSense\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"RealSense, a 3D perception technology company, sponsors AgenticROS, an open source project that connects NVIDIA Isaac ROS with NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints to let AI agents interact with ROS-based robots.\",\n  \"quote\": \"AgenticROS , an open source project sponsored by 3D perception technology company RealSense , connects Isaac ROS with NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints, enabling AI agents to interact with ROS-based robots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e3\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"RealSense\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"RealSense is optimizing its latest AI-native 3D stereo depth cameras, including the RealSense D585 Pro, and an open source software development kit for NVIDIA Isaac ROS and the NVIDIA Jetson Thor edge AI platform, aimed at perception, navigation and manipulation applications.\",\n  \"quote\": \"RealSense is also optimizing its latest AI-native 3D stereo depth cameras, including RealSense D585 Pro, and an open source software development kit for Isaac ROS and the NVIDIA Jetson Thor edge AI platform, helping developers build perception, navigation and manipulation applications.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e4\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Intrinsic\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Intrinsic released Intrinsic Core, an open source suite of preconfigured runtime services and capabilities for industrial robotics applications, and its Open Machine Tending Solution reference application for computer numerical control machine tending includes built-in compatibility with NVIDIA FoundationPose for object registration, tracking and pose estimation.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Intrinsic ’s Open Machine Tending Solution is a reference application for computer numerical control machine tending, part of the newly released Intrinsic Core , an open source suite of preconfigured runtime services and capabilities designed to accelerate industrial robotics applications . It includes built-in compatibility with NVIDIA FoundationPose for out-of-the-box object registration, tracking and pose estimation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e5\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Flexiv\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flexiv is integrating NVIDIA Isaac ROS with its Rizon 4 adaptive robot, giving developers NVIDIA-accelerated robotics capabilities and a path from testing applications in NVIDIA Isaac Sim to deploying them on a physical robot.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Flexiv is integrating Isaac ROS with its Rizon 4 adaptive robot, giving developers access to NVIDIA-accelerated robotics capabilities and a streamlined path from testing applications in NVIDIA Isaac Sim to deploying them on a physical robot.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e6\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Ouster\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Ouster is integrating its Stereolabs ZED stereo cameras with NVIDIA Isaac ROS to provide GPU-accelerated perception for robotics applications, aimed at real-time object detection, mapping and navigation while keeping interoperability with the broader ROS ecosystem.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Ouster integrates its Stereolabs ZED stereo cameras with NVIDIA Isaac ROS to deliver GPU-accelerated perception for robotics applications. The integration simplifies the development of real-time object detection, mapping and navigation while maintaining interoperability with the broader ROS ecosystem.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e7\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"ROBOTIS\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"ROBOTIS, the builder of the ROS-based TurtleBot3, is integrating NVIDIA Isaac ROS into its AI Worker robot, using GPU-accelerated object perception for vision-guided manipulation tasks including picking, placing and alignment.\",\n  \"quote\": \"ROBOTIS , which builds the developer-friendly ROS-based TurtleBot3, is integrating Isaac ROS into its AI Worker robot, using GPU-accelerated object perception to enable vision-guided manipulation tasks including picking, placing and alignment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e8\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"FieldAI\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NVIDIA Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"FieldAI is integrating NVIDIA Isaac ROS on Jetson devices into its robot foundation models, which run entirely on robots without cloud connectivity, to take greater advantage of GPU acceleration and improve on-robot AI stack efficiency.\",\n  \"quote\": \"FieldAI ’s robot foundation models, which can run entirely on robots without relying on cloud connectivity, are integrating Isaac ROS on Jetson devices to take greater advantage of GPU acceleration and improve the efficiency of the on-robot AI stack.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e9\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Sea Limited\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that Sea Limited is the first enterprise in the ASEAN region to adopt the NVIDIA Vera Rubin platform; Sea will use it to develop and deploy AI models and intelligent agents at greater scale across its businesses.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Sea Limited, a global technology company founded in Singapore, is the first enterprise in the ASEAN region to adopt the NVIDIA Vera Rubin platform , further strengthening the company’s AI capabilities to better serve and create meaningful economic opportunities for millions of consumers and small businesses across Southeast Asia. … Now, with NVIDIA Vera Rubin, Sea will build on these efforts, developing and deploying AI models and intelligent agents at greater scale to serve the evolving needs of its communities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e10\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"AI Singapore\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that AI Singapore is expanding its SEA-LION model family to include NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NeMo tools.\",\n  \"quote\": \"AI Singapore is expanding its SEA-LION model family to include the NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NeMo tools. SEA-LION is an open model family designed for Southeast Asian languages and cultures.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e11\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"HTX (Home Team Science and Technology Agency)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that Singapore’s HTX (Home Team Science and Technology Agency) is embarking on research using NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super and Nemotron 3 Nano Omni models for public-safety AI, with potential applications in complex reasoning, agentic workflows and multimodal operations.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Singapore’s HTX (Home Team Science and Technology Agency) is embarking on research using the NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super and Nemotron 3 Nano Omni models to advance AI for public safety. Nemotron Super has the potential to support the agency’s complex reasoning and agentic workflows, while Omni’s unified vision, audio and language capabilities could help HTX develop multimodal applications grounded in real-world operational data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e12\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NCS\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that NCS is advancing agentic AI adoption across enterprises and the public sector using Nemotron models and the NVIDIA Blueprint for video search and summarization, and is also advancing physical AI for practical humanoid robotics applications.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NCS is advancing agentic AI adoption across enterprises and the public sector, using Nemotron models and the NVIDIA Blueprint for video search and summarization (VSS) , while advancing physical AI for practical humanoid robotics applications, to address security, responsiveness and data governance requirements.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e13\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"ST Engineering\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that ST Engineering is using NVIDIA NeMo tools and cuOpt software to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy agentic AI solutions across its businesses, including Marine MRO.\",\n  \"quote\": \"ST Engineering is using NVIDIA NeMo tools and NVIDIA cuOpt software to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy agentic AI solutions across its businesses such as Marine MRO.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e14\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"YTL AI Labs\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that Malaysia’s YTL AI Labs is fine-tuning NVIDIA Nemotron models for enterprise and citizen services.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Malaysia’s YTL AI Labs is fine-tuning Nemotron models for enterprise and citizen services\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e15\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Viettel AI\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that Vietnam’s Viettel AI has been extensively fine-tuning NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super for Vietnamese-language and agentic applications, and the model is set to be adopted in its Legal AI agent harness for internal and external customers.\",\n  \"quote\": \"In Vietnam, Viettel AI has been extensively fine-tuning Nemotron 3 Super for the Vietnamese language and agentic applications. … and it’s set to be adopted in Legal AI — an agent harness that will serve both internal Viettel Group employees and external customers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e16\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"iApp Technology\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that in Thailand, iApp Technology, as part of the ThaiLLM Collaboration with the Big Data Institute, is adapting NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano by fine-tuning OpenThai 2.0 Legal with Thai-language legal data using the NVIDIA NeMo framework; the model is released as open source and powers its Thanoy legal-assistant chatbot, which already serves approximately 43,000 users.\",\n  \"quote\": \"In Thailand, the Big Data Institute and iApp Technology , as members of the ThaiLLM Collaboration, are exploring Nemotron as a foundation model. With an initial focus on legal applications, iApp Technology is adapting Nemotron 3 Nano by fine-tuning OpenThai 2.0 Legal with Thai-language legal data using the NVIDIA NeMo framework.\\nThe model is released as open source for the Thai developer community and serves as the engine for Thanoy, the company’s legal-assistant chatbot, which already serves approximately 43,000 users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e17\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Hummingbird Bioscience\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced that Hummingbird Bioscience, together with LynxKite, is building an explainable Toxicity Knowledge Graph powered by NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning and NeMo Retriever with in silico simulations, aiming to integrate public and proprietary data to accelerate drug discovery.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Hummingbird Bioscience, together with LynxKite, is building an explainable Toxicity Knowledge Graph powered by Nemotron 3.5 Lightning and NeMo Retriever with in silico simulations. The collaboration aims to integrate complex public and proprietary data across diverse third-party file formats, creating a comprehensive, unified foundation for robust analysis and reasoning that helps de-risk and accelerate drug discovery and development.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e18\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA management\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management expects roughly a quarter (about 25%) of the company's fiscal 2028 business to come from AI labs that NVIDIA will back with its own balance sheet.\",\n  \"quote\": \"If you hold NVIDIA (NVDA) stock, one number deserves your attention: roughly a quarter. That is the share of fiscal 2028 business management expects from AI labs it will back with its own balance sheet. … Roughly a quarter of expected fiscal 2028 business comes from AI labs NVIDIA plans to back.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e19\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's revenue more than doubled year over year in fiscal Q2 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA’s revenue more than doubled year over year in fiscal Q2 2027, so this number is easy to miss.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e20\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA management\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"According to management, NVIDIA has already invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA has already invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs, according to management.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e21\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Business Insider\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis, citing Business Insider\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Business Insider reported that NVIDIA's overall equity portfolio has reached $99 billion, up from roughly $7 billion in summer 2025 — a 14-fold increase.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Those lab investments are part of a broader expansion: Business Insider reported that NVIDIA’s overall equity portfolio has reached $99 billion. In summer 2025, that portfolio was roughly $7 billion. That is a 14-fold increase, so this is not a mild change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e22\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA plans to provide credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity for one additional AI lab.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For one more AI lab, it will provide credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e23\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guarantees a minimum level of revenue on part of a facility's capacity with some cloud partners.\",\n  \"quote\": \"With some cloud partners, it guarantees a minimum level of revenue on part of a facility’s capacity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e24\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis, citing NVIDIA management\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's days of sales outstanding, the average time to collect cash after a sale, increased to 60 days; management said this reflects extended payment terms for large purchases by certain investment-grade customers, shipped over multiple quarters.\",\n  \"quote\": \"There is also a change in how quickly NVIDIA gets paid. Days of sales outstanding, the average time to collect cash after a sale, increased to 60 days. Management said this reflects extended payment terms for large purchases by certain investment-grade customers, shipped over multiple quarters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e25\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"OpenAI\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Trefis, citing NVIDIA management\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"OpenAI's existing and planned commitments represent about 12 gigawatts of NVIDIA computing, and OpenAI has committed to deployments through 2030.\",\n  \"quote\": \"OpenAI’s existing and planned commitments represent about 12 gigawatts of NVIDIA computing. OpenAI has committed to deployments through 2030.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e26\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"In a comparison of AMD and NVIDIA, fool.com states that NVIDIA's sales more than doubled in its most recent quarter, presenting this as evidence NVIDIA is growing at a significantly faster rate than AMD; the item gives no revenue amount and does not label which quarter.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Meanwhile, even if its growth rate accelerates, it might not catch Nvidia, anyway -- its sales more than doubled in its most recent quarter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e27\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"fool.com reports that NVIDIA generated $192.9 billion in net income over the trailing 12 months, compared with $6.4 billion for AMD, citing this in a valuation comparison of the two AI chip makers.\",\n  \"quote\": \"AMD may be lighter in valuation, but so too are its profits; in the trailing 12 months, it has amassed $6.4 billion in net income while Nvidia has generated $192.9 billion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e28\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"AMD\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"fool.com reports that AMD, a competitor of NVIDIA in AI chips, came off a strong quarter for the period ending June 27 with revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"AMD is already coming off a strong quarter for the period ending June 27, with revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e29\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"AMD\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"AMD guided that for the current quarter (as of the 22 September 2026 article) it projects revenue growth of around 41%, a slightly slower rate than the 50% year-over-year growth it reported for the quarter ending June 27.\",\n  \"quote\": \"However, for the current quarter, it's projecting a slightly slower growth rate of around 41%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e30\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"AMD\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"AMD launched its new Helios rack-scale AI infrastructure system a few months before the 22 September 2026 article, and fool.com reports that the launch appears to have made investors bullish on AMD's ability to compete with NVIDIA, with high expectations that Helios will generate strong growth.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The launch of the company's new Helios rack-scale AI system appears to have investors bullish about AMD's ability to compete with Nvidia. AMD launched the AI infrastructure solution a few months ago, and expectations are high that it will generate strong growth.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e31\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA and Aolani\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA and Aolani agreed to deploy 22,000 GPUs across new AI factory sites in Southeast Asia, with the partners planning more than 100 megawatts of new AI factory capacity including major hubs in Malaysia and the Philippines; the article identifies the plan's marker as Aolani's early 2027 target to bring those 22,000 GPUs online at the planned 100 MW-plus capacity. NVIDIA is the GPU supplier and stack provider in the arrangement; the item gives no contract value, NVIDIA revenue, credit support or guarantee.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA (NasdaqGS: NVDA) and Aolani agreed to deploy 22,000 GPUs across new AI factory sites in Southeast Asia. … The partners plan over 100 megawatts of new AI factory capacity, including major hubs in Malaysia and the Philippines. … The key marker is whether Aolani meets its early 2027 target to bring those 22,000 GPUs online across Malaysia and the Philippines at the planned 100 megawatt plus capacity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e32\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Alphabet Inc. (Google)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Seoul Economic Daily\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-09\",\n  \"summary\": \"Google (Alphabet) met South Korean officials on September 9, 2026 to discuss supplying its tensor processing units (TPUs) for the country's sovereign-AI buildout, according to a September 22 report by Seoul Economic Daily; Google reportedly argues TPUs can lower AI-compute costs materially, though the article notes such claims depend on workload, software support and utilization. The article frames this as South Korea seeking less dependence on a single foreign supplier, in a sovereign-AI market where governments have leaned heavily on NVIDIA GPUs. No chip volumes, contract value or timeline were disclosed.\",\n  \"quote\": \"A September 22 report from Seoul Economic Daily said Google met South Korean officials on September 9 to discuss supplying tensor processing units for the country's sovereign-AI buildout. … Google reportedly argues that TPUs can lower AI-compute costs materially, but those claims depend on workload, software support and utilization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e33\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (zacks.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that sell-side consensus expects NVIDIA to post earnings of $2.47 per share in the current quarter, a +90% change from the year-ago quarter, and that the Zacks Consensus Estimate for that quarter has been revised up +5.8% over the last 30 days.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For the current quarter, Nvidia is expected to post earnings of $2.47 per share, indicating a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter. The Zacks Consensus Estimate has changed +5.8% over the last 30 days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e34\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (zacks.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that the consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's current fiscal year is $9.25, a +93.9% change from the prior year, and that this estimate has been revised up +5.1% over the last 30 days.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For the current fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $9.25 points to a change of +93.9% from the prior year. Over the last 30 days, this estimate has changed +5.1%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e35\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (zacks.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that the consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's next fiscal year is $15.33, indicating a +65.8% change from what the company is expected to report a year ago, and that this estimate has been revised up +21.8% over the past month.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For the next fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $15.33 indicates a change of +65.8% from what Nvidia is expected to report a year ago. Over the past month, the estimate has changed +21.8%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e36\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (zacks.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that the consensus sales estimate for NVIDIA's current quarter is $109.02 billion, indicating a +91.2% year-over-year change.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e37\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (zacks.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that consensus sales estimates for NVIDIA are $406.05 billion for the current fiscal year and $671.95 billion for the next fiscal year, indicating changes of +88% and +65.5% respectively.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For the current and next fiscal years, $406.05 billion and $671.95 billion estimates indicate +88% and +65.5% changes, respectively.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e38\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"SB Energy\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Financial Times (reported via Yahoo Finance)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"SB Energy, the SoftBank-backed developer, slowed preparations for a planned public listing that had been discussed around a $50 billion valuation, according to a September 22 Financial Times report, while a $4.9 billion debt package faced weak demand and yields around 10%.\",\n  \"quote\": \"SB Energy's planned public listing is turning into a stress test for the financing side of the AI buildout. The SoftBank-backed developer has slowed preparations for an IPO that had been discussed around a $50 billion valuation, according to a September 22 Financial Times report, while a $4.9 billion debt package has faced weak demand and yields around 10%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e39\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA had already invested $1.5 billion in SB Energy and committed another $1.5 billion tied to the developer's IPO.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) has already invested $1.5 billion and committed another $1.5 billion tied to the IPO.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e40\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"SB Energy\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"SB Energy (reported by Yahoo Finance)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"SB Energy said it has signed roughly 8.8 gigawatts of IT lease capacity, including the PORTS-Pike campus in Ohio for OpenAI, where NVIDIA is the exclusive AI-compute provider.\",\n  \"quote\": \"SB Energy says it has signed roughly 8.8 gigawatts of IT lease capacity, including the PORTS-Pike campus in Ohio for OpenAI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e41\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA is the exclusive AI-compute provider for SB Energy's PORTS-Pike campus in Ohio and is providing credit support for an initial 4.25 gigawatts of capacity there, with an option covering another 3.75 gigawatts.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia is the exclusive AI-compute provider for that site and is providing credit support for an initial 4.25 gigawatts, with an option covering another 3.75.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e42\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has disclosed maximum guarantee exposure that can reach $105 billion under defined conditions, tying its economics more closely to OpenAI's ability to meet its lease obligations.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia has disclosed maximum guarantee exposure that can reach $105 billion under defined conditions, so the economics become more intertwined with OpenAI's ability to meet its lease obligations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e43\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"GuruFocus\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's latest reported quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion in total revenue, so roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI, according to GuruFocus's recounting of the results in its 22 September 2026 article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"That is an eye-catching demonstration, but the scale gap remains enormous: Nvidia's latest quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion overall, meaning roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e44\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Zacks analyst (Zacks Investment Research)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks Research Daily\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"A Zacks analyst research report on NVIDIA, published in the 22 September 2026 Zacks Research Daily, stated that NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments, customer credit support and long-dated guarantees, while noting that China remains largely closed to data center compute. No amounts, counterparties or dates were given for the increased commitments.\",\n  \"quote\": \"China remains largely closed to data center compute, and NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments, customer credit support and long-dated guarantees.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e45\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"qz.com\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"qz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in the company's current fiscal year, according to expectations reported by qz.com; no individual forecaster is named for the growth figures (the item attributes the valuation data it cites to Bloomberg).\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e46\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"qz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"At the time of its second-quarter earnings, NVIDIA projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time, as reported by qz.com.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e47\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"qz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported that its revenue more than doubled in the second quarter, reported by qz.com in the context of its second-quarter earnings.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e48\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"qz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's gross margin came in at 75% in the last quarter, as reported by qz.com.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e49\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Bloomberg (analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"qz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show NVIDIA's gross margin sliding to under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter, as reported by qz.com; rising costs for key components such as memory chips are cited as a central factor.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e50\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Delos Data\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com (citing Reuters)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-15\",\n  \"summary\": \"Delos Data announced on 15 September 2026 that it raised more than $100 million to develop networking chips and software for increasingly heterogeneous AI data centres, with Playground Global — where former Intel CEO Pat Gelsinger is a general partner — joining the round; Reuters reported that Delos is designing its network to work across different types of compute hardware rather than assuming every accelerator comes from NVIDIA. The article frames this as an attempt to loosen Nvidia's integrated accelerator-networking-interconnect-software stack by making mixed AI clusters easier to build, while noting Delos is a startup attacking an incumbent that spends billions on research and still has to prove its claimed performance in commercial deployments.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Delos Data announced on September 15 that it raised more than $100 million to develop networking chips and software for increasingly heterogeneous AI data centers. Playground Global, where Gelsinger is a general partner, joined the round. Reuters reported that Delos is designing the network to work across different types of compute hardware rather than assuming every accelerator comes from NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ). … Delos is betting the market becomes less uniform as inference expands. Its pitch is that a data center should be able to connect whatever mix of accelerators makes economic sense.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e51\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Apple Inc.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"The Information (reported by finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-16\",\n  \"summary\": \"The Information reported on September 16 that Apple is developing enterprise servers built around future M8 Ultra processors, with designs under consideration using either two or four M8 Ultra chips and a possible 2029 launch aimed primarily at AI inference, and that Apple has also considered using NVIDIA's NVLink Fusion technology to connect those processors. The article states neither the server nor NVIDIA's involvement is finalized and the project could change or disappear.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The Information reported on September 16 that Apple Inc. (NASDAQ: AAPL ) is developing enterprise servers around future M8 Ultra processors. Designs under consideration use either two or four M8 Ultra chips, with a possible 2029 launch aimed primarily at AI inference. Apple has also considered NVIDIA Corporation's (NASDAQ: NVDA ) NVLink Fusion technology to connect those processors. … Neither the server nor Nvidia's involvement is finalized. The project could still change or disappear entirely.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e52\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"The Information\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"The Information (reported by finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The Information reported that networking equipment can represent 10% to 15% of AI data-center hardware costs, which the article says gives NVIDIA a revenue pool beyond GPUs.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The Information reported that networking equipment can represent 10% to 15% of AI data-center hardware costs, giving Nvidia a meaningful revenue pool beyond GPUs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e53\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Alibaba Group Holding Limited\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"Alibaba Group Holding used its 22 September 2026 developer conference to unveil the Zhenwu V900 AI accelerator, which Alibaba says delivers roughly three times the performance of its predecessor and which is scheduled for mass production in early 2027; the article notes the performance claims come from Alibaba and that mass production is still expected in 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Alibaba used its September 22 developer conference to show how quickly China's AI stack is filling the holes left by restricted access to U.S. chips. The company unveiled the Zhenwu V900 accelerator, which it says delivers roughly three times the performance of its predecessor and is scheduled for mass production in early 2027. … The obvious limitation is that the V900's performance claims come from Alibaba and mass production is still expected in 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e54\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Alibaba Group Holding Limited\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"At its 22 September 2026 developer conference, Alibaba Group Holding discussed future Qwen models scaling to 5 trillion to 10 trillion parameters and plans to expand its global data-center capacity above 20 gigawatts by 2032.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Alibaba Group Holding Limited (NYSE: BABA ) also discussed future Qwen models scaling to 5 trillion to 10 trillion parameters and its plans to expand global data-center capacity above 20 gigawatts by 2032. … The 20-gigawatt capacity target suggests the company is preparing for a much larger infrastructure footprint.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e55\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corp.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Brianna Wessling, The Robot Report\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA Corp. released Isaac ROS 5.0, its latest collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on the Robot Operating System open framework, announcing the release at the ROSCon conference in Toronto on 22 September 2026. Per NVIDIA, the release adds agentic workflows and platform support, support for ROS 2 Lyrical and Ubuntu 24.04, new Isaac Skills for setup and manipulation, a FoundationStereo fine-tuning skill, an agent-ready inference library for the FoundationPose object pose estimation and tracking model, and a standalone pick-and-place perception skill. The item discloses no revenue, pricing, orders or customer commitments tied to the release.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA Corp. today released Isaac ROS 5.0, its latest collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on the Robot Operating System open framework. The company announced the release at the ROSCon conference in Toronto. … The release brings new agentic workflows and platform support to help developers build, customize, and deploy robotics applications faster. … Isaac ROS 5.0 also introduces support for ROS 2 Lyrical and Ubuntu 24.04. … The release also includes new NVIDIA Isaac Skills for setup and manipulation. These provide reusable workflows that developers and AI agents can use to complete robotics development tasks. … As part of Isaac ROS 5.0, FoundationPose, a foundation model for object pose estimation and tracking, now provides an agent-ready inference library that enables robots to perceive and track the position and orientation of objects up to 5.5x faster.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e56\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue up 117% to $89 billion, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue surging 117% to $89 billion,\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e57\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management guided fiscal third-quarter revenue to approximately $108 billion, which the article says implies 89% growth.\",\n  \"quote\": \"management has guided for approximately $108 billion in third-quarter revenue, implying 89% growth\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e58\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CEO Jensen Huang)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang has projected that the company's chip sales could double in calendar year 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"CEO Jensen Huang has projected that chip sales could double in calendar year 2027,\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e59\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, a figure the article says far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled.\",\n  \"quote\": \"while CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — a figure that far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e60\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"barchart.com (article analysis)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that NVIDIA is financing a growing share of its sales to AI startups, with roughly 25% of fiscal 2028 revenue expected to come from customers receiving some form of company-backed financing — potentially $175 billion funded off NVIDIA's own balance sheet.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia is financing a growing share of its sales to AI startups, with roughly 25% of fiscal 2028 revenue expected to come from customers receiving some form of company-backed financing — potentially $175 billion funded off its own balance sheet.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e61\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"barchart.com (article analysis)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article states that NVIDIA has off-balance-sheet guarantees exceeding $100 billion tied to projects such as the SB Energy campus for OpenAI, which it says introduces credit risk that traditional valuation metrics do not capture.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Additionally, off-balance-sheet guarantees exceeding $100 billion tied to projects like the SB Energy campus for OpenAI introduce credit risk that traditional valuation metrics do not capture.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e62\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Sell-side analyst consensus (as reported by barchart.com)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that analysts' consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA has been revised sharply higher, from $8.50 to $15.68 per share for fiscal 2029, over just the past nine months.\",\n  \"quote\": \"earnings estimates that have been revised sharply higher — from $8.50 to $15.68 per share for fiscal 2029 — over just the past nine months\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e63\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Sea\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"sg.finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Singapore-founded consumer-internet group Sea said it will adopt NVIDIA's Vera Rubin computing platform to build and deploy AI models and agents at greater scale across its Shopee, Monee and Garena businesses, saying it will use Vera Rubin to extend AI work already under way there; the item gives no deployment timing, capacity, volumes or contract value.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Singapore-founded Sea will adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform to build and deploy artificial-intelligence (AI) models and agents at greater scale across its Shopee, Monee and Garena businesses. … Vera Rubin is a computing platform that provides the processing capacity to develop and run AI systems. Sea says it will use Vera Rubin to extend AI work already underway at its businesses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e64\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Sea (Shopee)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"sg.finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Sea's e-commerce arm Shopee runs Compass, an in-house AI model built and run on NVIDIA graphics processors and software, which powers search, product recommendations, fraud checks and customer service; the item reports that over eight months Compass's monthly processing volume rose from 3 billion to 340 billion tokens, that it now accounts for most of Shopee's AI traffic, and that it made fraud detection 50 times more efficient than manual review and cut processing costs by 90%.\",\n  \"quote\": \"At Shopee, Compass is an in-house AI model built and run on Nvidia graphics processors and software. It powers search, product recommendations, fraud checks and customer service. … Over eight months, Compass's monthly processing volume rose from 3 billion to 340 billion tokens. Tokens are the units of text an AI model reads and generates. Compass now accounts for most of Shopee's AI traffic. It has also made fraud detection 50 times more efficient than manual review and cut processing costs by 90%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e65\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"CyberPowerPC\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"videocardz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"System builder CyberPowerPC is now shipping prebuilt gaming PCs equipped with NVIDIA's own GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition graphics cards (RTX 5070 or RTX 5080 Founders Edition), sold through Walmart as part of the retailer's GeForce Week promotion running 21–27 September 2026; the article notes Founders Edition cards are normally associated with NVIDIA's own retail channel and selected retailers while prebuilt systems commonly use board-partner cards, so these systems give buyers another route to NVIDIA's own RTX 5070/5080 design without purchasing the card separately. Four CyberPowerPC configurations carried the Founders Edition cards in Walmart listings.\",\n  \"quote\": \"CyberPowerPC is now shipping prebuilt gaming PCs with NVIDIA’s own GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition graphics cards. The systems are being sold through Walmart as part of the retailer’s GeForce Week promotion, which runs from September 21 through September 27. … Walmart currently lists four CyberPowerPC systems with either the GeForce RTX 5070 Founders Edition or RTX 5080 Founders Edition. … Founders Edition cards are normally associated with NVIDIA’s own retail channel and selected retailers, while prebuilt systems commonly use graphics cards from board partners. These CyberPowerPC systems therefore provide another way to obtain NVIDIA’s own RTX 5070 or RTX 5080 design without buying the graphics card separately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e66\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"videocardz.com\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"videocardz.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"According to the article's author, the $2,299 CyberPowerPC system pairing an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 Founders Edition with a Ryzen 7 9800X3D and 32GB DDR5-6000 memory (Walmart listing SLC8500WST) sold out in one day with over 1,000 orders; the author reads this as consistent with how much RTX 5080 cards currently cost. The unit count is the author's report of the retailer listing, not an NVIDIA disclosure.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The Ryzen 7 9800X3D configuration is probably the one attracting the most attention. Walmart lists the SLC8500WST with an RTX 5080 Founders Edition, 32GB DDR5-6000 memory and a $2,299 price. … I think the $2,299 system that sold out in one day with over 1,000 orders makes sense given how much RTX 5080 cards cost now.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e67\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"CyberPowerPC / Walmart\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"TweakTown (citing VideoCardz)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"CyberPowerPC listed prebuilt gaming PCs equipped with NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 and RTX 5070 Founders Edition GPUs on Walmart as part of the retailer's NVIDIA GeForce promotion this week; the RTX 5080 configurations ($2,299 with a Ryzen 9800X3D and $2,399 with an Intel Core Ultra 9 285K) sold out within about a day, with Walmart reportedly moving over 1,000 units, while the two RTX 5070 systems ($1,599 with a Ryzen 7800X3D and $1,549 with an Intel 14700KF) remained in stock.\",\n  \"quote\": \"CyberPowerPC listed prebuilt PCs with NVIDIA RTX 5080 and 5070 Founders Edition GPUs at Walmart, but the RTX 5080 rigs sold out very quickly - in just a day, in fact (with over 1,000 units moved). Two RTX 5070 PCs remain available at $1,599 and $1,549. … VideoCardz reports that the manufacturer of prebuilts is selling PCs with Founders Edition RTX 5080 and 5070 GPUs inside them via Walmart , as part of the retailer's NVIDIA GeForce promotion this week. … According to VideoCardz, the cheaper RTX 5080 systems sold out in a day flat, with Walmart shifting over 1,000 units apparently.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e68\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n  \"said_by\": \"TweakTown\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"TweakTown\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"TweakTown reported that third-party NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 graphics cards were selling for around $850 in the US, up from around $650 a couple of months earlier, with GPU pricing worsening because of a memory (RAM) shortage; it said standalone third-party RTX 5080 cards now start at about $1,500 in the US.\",\n  \"quote\": \"I expect the RTX 5070 PCs will last longer - they're both still in stock at the time of writing - but even these represent a decent bargain given that you're looking at around $850 for a third-party card in the US these days. That's up from around $650 just a couple of months ago, and GPU pricing is getting a whole lot worse thanks to the RAM crisis. … It's hardly surprising that the RTX 5080 PCs flew off the shelves at Walmart, given that the standalone graphics card now costs from $1,500 upwards in the US.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e69\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Sakeena Fiza, NVIDIA validation engineer, in an NVIDIA Blog post\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA validation engineer Sakeena Fiza, writing in an NVIDIA corporate blog post, said she saw the NVIDIA Rubin GPU working at system level for the first time in the company's data center systems engineering lab, the first time a Rubin GPU has enumerated at system level; she describes validation as work done on a device before mass production begins and before customers depend on it. The item gives no date for the milestone, no quantities, no shipment or production timing and no customer or revenue detail.\",\n  \"quote\": \"One of Fiza’s earliest and most enduring memories of working at NVIDIA is the collective joy she experienced when she saw the NVIDIA Rubin GPU working for the first time at a system level. … “It literally just said, ‘NVIDIA Corporation Device,’” she recalls. “And everyone’s cheering and celebrating because it’s the first time in the world that a Rubin GPU enumerated at a system level.” … Fiza describes validation — the process of ensuring a physical device works correctly before mass production begins — as becoming “the first customers for the product,” exercising hardware to its limits in a range of real-world conditions before anyone else has to depend on it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e70\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Sea Group (Li Kuangli, senior director of partnerships and strategy) and Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"computerweekly.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"At Nvidia AI Day Singapore, Sea Group senior director of partnerships and strategy Li Kuangli said Sea Group will be the first enterprise in Southeast Asia to adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform (Nvidia's Vera CPU combined with Rubin GPUs), as part of an AI strategy in which Sea runs every layer of its technology stack except the chips. The companies said Vera Rubin will allow Sea to build and deploy AI models and agents at a larger scale, but did not say how large the deployment will be or when it will go live.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Sea Group will be the first enterprise in Southeast Asia to adopt Nvidia’s Vera Rubin platform , building on an artificial intelligence (AI) strategy that lets it run every layer of its technology stack except the chips. … The companies said Vera Rubin, which combines Nvidia’s Vera central processing unit (CPU) with its Rubin graphics processing units (GPUs), will allow Sea to build and deploy AI models and agents at a larger scale. They did not say how big the deployment will be, or when it will go live.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e71\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Sea Group (Li Kuangli)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"computerweekly.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Sea Group senior director of partnerships and strategy Li Kuangli disclosed that Sea runs its own datacentre infrastructure of over 150,000 servers and more than 25,000 GPUs across 40-plus datacentres worldwide, with a combined critical IT load in excess of 100MW; the network has more than 120 interconnections with tier-one internet service providers and handles over 1.1 exabytes of traffic a month (about 700 million hours of high-definition video, by Li's calculation).\",\n  \"quote\": \"On top of the chips is infrastructure that Sea runs itself: over 150,000 servers and more than 25,000 GPUs across 40-plus datacentres worldwide, with a combined critical IT load in excess of 100MW. The network has more than 120 interconnections with tier-one internet service providers, and handles over 1.1 exabytes of traffic a month – about 700 million hours of high-definition video, by Li’s calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e72\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"AI Singapore (William Tjhi)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"computerweekly.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"William Tjhi, head of applied research at AI Singapore (AISG), said AISG — creator of the Sea-Lion family of open models for Southeast Asian languages — is expanding Sea-Lion with Nvidia's Nemotron open models and NeMo tools.\",\n  \"quote\": \"AISG, creator of the Sea-Lion family of open models for Southeast Asian languages, is expanding it with Nvidia’s Nemotron open models and NeMo tools.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e73\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia (Marc Hamilton)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"computerweekly.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia vice-president of solutions architecture and engineering Marc Hamilton, speaking at Nvidia AI Day Singapore, showed GitHub data in which new repositories had climbed to 20 million a month by April, which he attributed to growing use of coding agents; he said such agents can run thousands of inferences on a single task and that some AI-native companies burnt through their annual coding budgets in the first month or two of this year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Marc Hamilton, vice-president of solutions architecture and engineering at Nvidia, showed GitHub data in which new repositories had climbed to 20 million a month by April, which he attributed to the growing use of coding agents . Those agents can run thousands of inferences on a single task, and some AI-native companies burnt through their annual coding budgets in the first month or two of this year, he said.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e74\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Andriy Myronenko, Supriya V. Thathachary and Monty Zarrouk (NVIDIA Technical Blog)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced on its developer blog the open release of NV-Reason-CT, a vision-language model purpose-built for 3D CT analysis that combines a full 3D vision transformer encoder with a Qwen3.5-4B language model to generate radiologist-style chain-of-thought reasoning and structured reports; NVIDIA says the model is now openly available for research and development, with weights on Hugging Face and code on GitHub. NVIDIA describes it as an open research and development foundation, not an autonomous diagnostic system or a cleared clinical product, and reports state-of-the-art CT-RATE benchmark results (Macro-F1 0.614, Macro-AUROC 0.871) versus published 3D contrastive and fused 2D/3D baselines. No revenue, pricing, customer order or capacity commitment is attached to the release.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NV-Reason-CXR reasoning methodology extends to 3D CT analysis with NV-Reason-CT, a vision language model purpose-built for volumetric imaging. … NV-Reason-CT is an open research and development foundation; not an autonomous diagnostic system or a cleared clinical product. It is an AI foundation model designed for researchers and developers building specialized CT analysis applications to post-train for their use case. … NV-Reason-CT achieves state-of-the-art results on the CT-RATE benchmark with a Macro-F1 of 0.614 and Macro-AUROC of 0.871, outperforming published 3D contrastive and fused 2D/3D baselines. … Ready to get started? The model is now openly available for research and development.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e75\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"IonQ press release (ionq.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced on 23 September 2026 that it will make the first on-premise quantum computing deployment at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC): an IonQ Superion 256 system will be installed at the facility and directly linked to an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 system via NVIDIA NVQLink, with workloads orchestrated by the open NVIDIA CUDA-Q platform, under a joint research program on hybrid software development and large-scale system prototyping. IonQ said installation at NVAQC is scheduled for next year (2027).\",\n  \"quote\": \"Today, IonQ (NYSE: IONQ) announced that it will be the first on-premise quantum computing deployment at the NVIDIA Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC). … As part of the partnership, an IonQ Superion 256 system will be installed at the NVAQC and directly linked with an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 system via NVIDIA NVQLink , with workloads orchestrated by the open NVIDIA CUDA-Q platform. … The joint research program will focus on hybrid software development and large-scale system prototyping, generating open results and a guide for future AI use cases and quantum-GPU co-design. … Installation at NVAQC is scheduled for next year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e76\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Morningstar article author\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia told shareholders in May 2026 that it would raise its quarterly dividend to $0.25 per share from $0.01 per share, an increase the Morningstar author calculates at 2,400%. The author estimates roughly $25 billion per year would be returned to shareholders through the dividend, which would make Nvidia one of the largest dividend payers in the US market; that annual figure is the author's approximation, not a company-disclosed total.\",\n  \"quote\": \"In May, Nvidia told shareholders that it would increase its quarterly payout to $0.25 per share from $0.01 per share. That’s a 2,400% increase, according to my calculations! … But in absolute terms, Nvidia’s dividend is huge. Something like $25 billion per year will be returned to shareholders. That sum will make Nvidia one of the largest dividend payers in the US stock market.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e77\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Morningstar article author\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia announced an $80 billion share buyback program at the time of its May 2026 dividend declaration, per the Morningstar article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Indeed, Nvidia announced an $80 billion share buyback program at the time of its dividend declaration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e78\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Morningstar article author\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Morningstar, recapping the year's Nvidia news in September 2026, refers to Nvidia's forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth, without stating the period or scope those forecasts cover. The article gives the forecast as context for how Nvidia's valuation and growth profile sit against its dividend.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Lost in a torrent of news about Nvidia NVDA this year—its role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments , its forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth , and its acquisition of Hugging Face —was a dividend announcement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e79\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Morningstar article author\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Morningstar, listing the year's major Nvidia news in September 2026, describes Nvidia's \\\"role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments\\\" as one of the threads around which its dividend announcement was overlooked. The article does not specify the form of that financing (equity, debt, credit support or guarantees), the counterparties, or the period covered.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Lost in a torrent of news about Nvidia NVDA this year—its role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments , its forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth , and its acquisition of Hugging Face —was a dividend announcement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e80\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"The Trump administration (U.S. government)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The Trump administration has allowed Nvidia to ship its H200 AI chips to approved customers in China, per the article; the H200 is described as an older-generation product behind Nvidia's current Blackwell chips.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The Trump administration has allowed Nvidia to ship its H200 AI chips to approved customers in China.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e81\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Chinese authorities\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Chinese authorities have so far restricted shipments of Nvidia's H200 chips into China, according to the article, despite U.S. permission for those shipments to approved customers.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Chinese authorities, however, have so far restricted shipments of Nvidia's H200 chips.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e82\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia has not factored any sales from China into its outlook for the year, according to the article — meaning any resumption of China shipments would be incremental to its stated outlook.\",\n  \"quote\": \"While Nvidia hasn't factored any sales from China into its outlook for the year, the stock is still up 21% year to date, powered by the AI boom here in the US.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e83\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter 2027 consolidated revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, with Data Center segment revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, and non-GAAP gross margin of 75% versus 72.5% a year earlier, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release as cited by Zacks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The Data Center segment remains NVIDIA's primary growth engine, with revenues jumping 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the Aug. 26 press release. Consolidated revenues soared to $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially. … NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin increased to 75% in the fiscal second quarter compared with 72.5% a year ago.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e84\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, which at the midpoint would represent a 12% sequential increase, as cited by Zacks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA further expects profitability to remain strong and projects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in the fiscal third quarter of 2027. At the midpoint, this would represent a 12% sequential rise.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e85\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform has entered the full production stage, positioning the company to benefit from the next phase of AI infrastructure investment, as reported by Zacks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Additionally, the next-generation Vera Rubin platform has entered the full production stage, positioning NVIDIA to benefit from the next phase of AI infrastructure investment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e86\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Jensen Huang (NVIDIA CEO)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang is scheduled to attend President Donald Trump's state dinner for Chinese President Xi Jinping on Sept. 24, 2026, along with other technology leaders, as the U.S. and China discuss AI, trade, tariffs and advanced semiconductors. The article says the dinner itself does not guarantee policy changes but could provide a backdrop for signals on NVIDIA's access to the Chinese market and export restrictions.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia (NVDA) investors have a key date to watch as CEO Jensen Huang is set to attend President Donald Trump's state dinner for Chinese President Xi Jinping on Sept. 24, along with other prominent technology leaders at the White House. The high-profile gathering comes as the U.S. and China navigate sensitive issues involving artificial intelligence (AI), trade, tariffs, and advanced semiconductor technology. … Huang's presence is particularly notable for Nvidia, given the company's position at the center of the global AI chip market and the ongoing U.S.-China technology relationship. Investors will be watching whether discussions around AI and semiconductor trade create any signals relevant to Nvidia's access to the Chinese market, export restrictions, or the broader outlook for AI infrastructure demand. … While the dinner itself does not guarantee any policy changes, Sept. 24 could provide an important backdrop for Nvidia stock as the market weighs the potential implications of renewed U.S.-China engagement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e87\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, 2026, for the quarter ended July 26: revenue rose 106% year over year to a record $96.2 billion (up 18% sequentially) and exceeded prior guidance of $91 billion plus or minus 2%. Non-GAAP net income rose 118% to $54 billion, adjusted EPS rose 120% to $2.22, non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%, and operating income rose 124% to $63.7 billion. Data Center revenue was $89 billion, up 117% year over year and the majority of total revenue.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%. … The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion. … Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e88\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, and GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins to approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points. The forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Furthermore, Nvidia issued an even stronger outlook. For Q3 fiscal 2027, the company expects revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. Importantly, the forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China. Nvidia expects GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e89\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nebius Group; CoreWeave\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nebius Group announced another increase in prices for NVIDIA GPU rentals, and CoreWeave said it was continuing to contract new compute capacity at higher prices; the article cites both as fresh evidence that demand for NVIDIA-powered computing remains strong. No price levels, capacity amounts or dates are given.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Meanwhile, demand from AI cloud providers remains robust as Nebius Group (NBIS) announced another increase in prices for Nvidia GPU rentals, while CoreWeave (CRWV) said it was continuing to contract new compute capacity at higher prices, providing fresh evidence that demand for Nvidia-powered computing remains strong.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e90\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA management\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management pointed to full production of its next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform, and the article says continued AI infrastructure strength is accelerating NVIDIA's AI growth trajectory. The statement does not say Vera Rubin has begun volume customer shipments or revenue recognition.\",\n  \"quote\": \"It's worth noting that Nvidia is not merely maintaining its AI growth trajectory; it is accelerating it, with management pointing to full production of its next-generation Vera Rubin platform and continued strength across AI infrastructure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e91\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Street analysts (consensus)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"Street analysts expect NVIDIA's EPS to grow 102.4% year over year to $9.25 in fiscal 2027, followed by another 65.7% increase to $15.33 in fiscal 2028, according to the article's consensus forecast.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Street expects Nvidia's momentum to continue, with analysts forecasting EPS growth of 102.4% YoY to $9.25 in fiscal 2027, followed by another 65.7% increase to $15.33 in fiscal 2028.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e92\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nscale\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com (article, no byline)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-18\",\n  \"summary\": \"AI cloud provider Nscale filed for a U.S. initial public offering on 18 September 2026 disclosing that it lost $1.02 billion in the first six months of 2026 on revenue of just $140.6 million — the financial condition of the counterparty to which NVIDIA is committing $1 billion of convertible financing.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nscale filed for a U.S. initial public offering on September 18 with one number that makes the AI-cloud boom look radioactive: the company lost $1.02 billion in the first six months of 2026 on just $140.6 million of revenue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e93\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com (article, no byline)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA is committing $1 billion to a $3.1 billion convertible financing for AI cloud provider Nscale, the IPO candidate whose filing the article discusses; the article notes this gives NVIDIA direct capital exposure in addition to its role as hardware supplier.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Yet NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) is committing $1 billion to a $3.1 billion convertible financing, while Microsoft Corporation (NASDAQ: MSFT ) is expected to become one of Nscale's most important customers. … Nvidia can still benefit from Nscale's expansion by selling the picks and shovels, although its $1 billion financing commitment gives it direct capital exposure as well.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e94\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nscale\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com (article, no byline)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-18\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nscale disclosed that as of 31 August 2026 it had $103.4 billion of active and contracted total contract value under long-term take-or-pay contracts with a weighted-average contract life of about 5.7 years, operating in 14 regions with more than 10 gigawatts of potential power capacity — the contracted demand base underlying the Nscale build-out NVIDIA supplies and is financing.\",\n  \"quote\": \"As of August 31, Nscale had $103.4 billion of active and contracted total contract value under long-term take-or-pay contracts, with a weighted-average contract life of about 5.7 years. It operates in 14 regions and has more than 10 gigawatts of potential power capacity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e95\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nscale\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com (article, no byline)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-18\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nscale disclosed that a single customer generated 52% of its first-half 2026 revenue, and its future plan leans heavily on Microsoft and Anthropic, indicating concentrated demand behind its contract book.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nscale disclosed that one customer generated 52% of first-half revenue, and its future plan leans heavily on Microsoft and Anthropic.\"\n }\n]","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part1.json\\\"; a=json.load(open(p)); [print(x[\\\"statement\\\"]+\\\" \\\"+x[\\\"summary\\\"]) for x in a]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part1.json\\\"; a=json.load(open(p)); [print(x[\\\"statement\\\"]+\\\" \\\"+x[\\\"summary\\\"]) for x in a]'\"","aggregated_output":"e1 NVIDIA released Isaac ROS 5.0, a collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on ROS, at the ROSCon conference in Toronto; the release is free and open source, adds support for ROS Lyrical and Ubuntu 24.04, and scales across compute from Jetson Orin Nano to Jetson Thor.\ne2 RealSense, a 3D perception technology company, sponsors AgenticROS, an open source project that connects NVIDIA Isaac ROS with NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints to let AI agents interact with ROS-based robots.\ne3 RealSense is optimizing its latest AI-native 3D stereo depth cameras, including the RealSense D585 Pro, and an open source software development kit for NVIDIA Isaac ROS and the NVIDIA Jetson Thor edge AI platform, aimed at perception, navigation and manipulation applications.\ne4 Intrinsic released Intrinsic Core, an open source suite of preconfigured runtime services and capabilities for industrial robotics applications, and its Open Machine Tending Solution reference application for computer numerical control machine tending includes built-in compatibility with NVIDIA FoundationPose for object registration, tracking and pose estimation.\ne5 Flexiv is integrating NVIDIA Isaac ROS with its Rizon 4 adaptive robot, giving developers NVIDIA-accelerated robotics capabilities and a path from testing applications in NVIDIA Isaac Sim to deploying them on a physical robot.\ne6 Ouster is integrating its Stereolabs ZED stereo cameras with NVIDIA Isaac ROS to provide GPU-accelerated perception for robotics applications, aimed at real-time object detection, mapping and navigation while keeping interoperability with the broader ROS ecosystem.\ne7 ROBOTIS, the builder of the ROS-based TurtleBot3, is integrating NVIDIA Isaac ROS into its AI Worker robot, using GPU-accelerated object perception for vision-guided manipulation tasks including picking, placing and alignment.\ne8 FieldAI is integrating NVIDIA Isaac ROS on Jetson devices into its robot foundation models, which run entirely on robots without cloud connectivity, to take greater advantage of GPU acceleration and improve on-robot AI stack efficiency.\ne9 NVIDIA announced that Sea Limited is the first enterprise in the ASEAN region to adopt the NVIDIA Vera Rubin platform; Sea will use it to develop and deploy AI models and intelligent agents at greater scale across its businesses.\ne10 NVIDIA announced that AI Singapore is expanding its SEA-LION model family to include NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NeMo tools.\ne11 NVIDIA announced that Singapore’s HTX (Home Team Science and Technology Agency) is embarking on research using NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super and Nemotron 3 Nano Omni models for public-safety AI, with potential applications in complex reasoning, agentic workflows and multimodal operations.\ne12 NVIDIA announced that NCS is advancing agentic AI adoption across enterprises and the public sector using Nemotron models and the NVIDIA Blueprint for video search and summarization, and is also advancing physical AI for practical humanoid robotics applications.\ne13 NVIDIA announced that ST Engineering is using NVIDIA NeMo tools and cuOpt software to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy agentic AI solutions across its businesses, including Marine MRO.\ne14 NVIDIA announced that Malaysia’s YTL AI Labs is fine-tuning NVIDIA Nemotron models for enterprise and citizen services.\ne15 NVIDIA announced that Vietnam’s Viettel AI has been extensively fine-tuning NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super for Vietnamese-language and agentic applications, and the model is set to be adopted in its Legal AI agent harness for internal and external customers.\ne16 NVIDIA announced that in Thailand, iApp Technology, as part of the ThaiLLM Collaboration with the Big Data Institute, is adapting NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano by fine-tuning OpenThai 2.0 Legal with Thai-language legal data using the NVIDIA NeMo framework; the model is released as open source and powers its Thanoy legal-assistant chatbot, which already serves approximately 43,000 users.\ne17 NVIDIA announced that Hummingbird Bioscience, together with LynxKite, is building an explainable Toxicity Knowledge Graph powered by NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning and NeMo Retriever with in silico simulations, aiming to integrate public and proprietary data to accelerate drug discovery.\ne18 NVIDIA management expects roughly a quarter (about 25%) of the company's fiscal 2028 business to come from AI labs that NVIDIA will back with its own balance sheet.\ne19 NVIDIA's revenue more than doubled year over year in fiscal Q2 2027.\ne20 According to management, NVIDIA has already invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs.\ne21 Business Insider reported that NVIDIA's overall equity portfolio has reached $99 billion, up from roughly $7 billion in summer 2025 — a 14-fold increase.\ne22 NVIDIA plans to provide credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity for one additional AI lab.\ne23 NVIDIA guarantees a minimum level of revenue on part of a facility's capacity with some cloud partners.\ne24 NVIDIA's days of sales outstanding, the average time to collect cash after a sale, increased to 60 days; management said this reflects extended payment terms for large purchases by certain investment-grade customers, shipped over multiple quarters.\ne25 OpenAI's existing and planned commitments represent about 12 gigawatts of NVIDIA computing, and OpenAI has committed to deployments through 2030.\ne26 In a comparison of AMD and NVIDIA, fool.com states that NVIDIA's sales more than doubled in its most recent quarter, presenting this as evidence NVIDIA is growing at a significantly faster rate than AMD; the item gives no revenue amount and does not label which quarter.\ne27 fool.com reports that NVIDIA generated $192.9 billion in net income over the trailing 12 months, compared with $6.4 billion for AMD, citing this in a valuation comparison of the two AI chip makers.\ne28 fool.com reports that AMD, a competitor of NVIDIA in AI chips, came off a strong quarter for the period ending June 27 with revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year.\ne29 AMD guided that for the current quarter (as of the 22 September 2026 article) it projects revenue growth of around 41%, a slightly slower rate than the 50% year-over-year growth it reported for the quarter ending June 27.\ne30 AMD launched its new Helios rack-scale AI infrastructure system a few months before the 22 September 2026 article, and fool.com reports that the launch appears to have made investors bullish on AMD's ability to compete with NVIDIA, with high expectations that Helios will generate strong growth.\ne31 NVIDIA and Aolani agreed to deploy 22,000 GPUs across new AI factory sites in Southeast Asia, with the partners planning more than 100 megawatts of new AI factory capacity including major hubs in Malaysia and the Philippines; the article identifies the plan's marker as Aolani's early 2027 target to bring those 22,000 GPUs online at the planned 100 MW-plus capacity. NVIDIA is the GPU supplier and stack provider in the arrangement; the item gives no contract value, NVIDIA revenue, credit support or guarantee.\ne32 Google (Alphabet) met South Korean officials on September 9, 2026 to discuss supplying its tensor processing units (TPUs) for the country's sovereign-AI buildout, according to a September 22 report by Seoul Economic Daily; Google reportedly argues TPUs can lower AI-compute costs materially, though the article notes such claims depend on workload, software support and utilization. The article frames this as South Korea seeking less dependence on a single foreign supplier, in a sovereign-AI market where governments have leaned heavily on NVIDIA GPUs. No chip volumes, contract value or timeline were disclosed.\ne33 Zacks reported that sell-side consensus expects NVIDIA to post earnings of $2.47 per share in the current quarter, a +90% change from the year-ago quarter, and that the Zacks Consensus Estimate for that quarter has been revised up +5.8% over the last 30 days.\ne34 Zacks reported that the consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's current fiscal year is $9.25, a +93.9% change from the prior year, and that this estimate has been revised up +5.1% over the last 30 days.\ne35 Zacks reported that the consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's next fiscal year is $15.33, indicating a +65.8% change from what the company is expected to report a year ago, and that this estimate has been revised up +21.8% over the past month.\ne36 Zacks reported that the consensus sales estimate for NVIDIA's current quarter is $109.02 billion, indicating a +91.2% year-over-year change.\ne37 Zacks reported that consensus sales estimates for NVIDIA are $406.05 billion for the current fiscal year and $671.95 billion for the next fiscal year, indicating changes of +88% and +65.5% respectively.\ne38 SB Energy, the SoftBank-backed developer, slowed preparations for a planned public listing that had been discussed around a $50 billion valuation, according to a September 22 Financial Times report, while a $4.9 billion debt package faced weak demand and yields around 10%.\ne39 NVIDIA had already invested $1.5 billion in SB Energy and committed another $1.5 billion tied to the developer's IPO.\ne40 SB Energy said it has signed roughly 8.8 gigawatts of IT lease capacity, including the PORTS-Pike campus in Ohio for OpenAI, where NVIDIA is the exclusive AI-compute provider.\ne41 NVIDIA is the exclusive AI-compute provider for SB Energy's PORTS-Pike campus in Ohio and is providing credit support for an initial 4.25 gigawatts of capacity there, with an option covering another 3.75 gigawatts.\ne42 NVIDIA has disclosed maximum guarantee exposure that can reach $105 billion under defined conditions, tying its economics more closely to OpenAI's ability to meet its lease obligations.\ne43 NVIDIA's latest reported quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion in total revenue, so roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI, according to GuruFocus's recounting of the results in its 22 September 2026 article.\ne44 A Zacks analyst research report on NVIDIA, published in the 22 September 2026 Zacks Research Daily, stated that NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments, customer credit support and long-dated guarantees, while noting that China remains largely closed to data center compute. No amounts, counterparties or dates were given for the increased commitments.\ne45 NVIDIA's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in the company's current fiscal year, according to expectations reported by qz.com; no individual forecaster is named for the growth figures (the item attributes the valuation data it cites to Bloomberg).\ne46 At the time of its second-quarter earnings, NVIDIA projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time, as reported by qz.com.\ne47 NVIDIA reported that its revenue more than doubled in the second quarter, reported by qz.com in the context of its second-quarter earnings.\ne48 NVIDIA's gross margin came in at 75% in the last quarter, as reported by qz.com.\ne49 Analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show NVIDIA's gross margin sliding to under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter, as reported by qz.com; rising costs for key components such as memory chips are cited as a central factor.\ne50 Delos Data announced on 15 September 2026 that it raised more than $100 million to develop networking chips and software for increasingly heterogeneous AI data centres, with Playground Global — where former Intel CEO Pat Gelsinger is a general partner — joining the round; Reuters reported that Delos is designing its network to work across different types of compute hardware rather than assuming every accelerator comes from NVIDIA. The article frames this as an attempt to loosen Nvidia's integrated accelerator-networking-interconnect-software stack by making mixed AI clusters easier to build, while noting Delos is a startup attacking an incumbent that spends billions on research and still has to prove its claimed performance in commercial deployments.\ne51 The Information reported on September 16 that Apple is developing enterprise servers built around future M8 Ultra processors, with designs under consideration using either two or four M8 Ultra chips and a possible 2029 launch aimed primarily at AI inference, and that Apple has also considered using NVIDIA's NVLink Fusion technology to connect those processors. The article states neither the server nor NVIDIA's involvement is finalized and the project could change or disappear.\ne52 The Information reported that networking equipment can represent 10% to 15% of AI data-center hardware costs, which the article says gives NVIDIA a revenue pool beyond GPUs.\ne53 Alibaba Group Holding used its 22 September 2026 developer conference to unveil the Zhenwu V900 AI accelerator, which Alibaba says delivers roughly three times the performance of its predecessor and which is scheduled for mass production in early 2027; the article notes the performance claims come from Alibaba and that mass production is still expected in 2027.\ne54 At its 22 September 2026 developer conference, Alibaba Group Holding discussed future Qwen models scaling to 5 trillion to 10 trillion parameters and plans to expand its global data-center capacity above 20 gigawatts by 2032.\ne55 NVIDIA Corp. released Isaac ROS 5.0, its latest collection of GPU-accelerated packages built on the Robot Operating System open framework, announcing the release at the ROSCon conference in Toronto on 22 September 2026. Per NVIDIA, the release adds agentic workflows and platform support, support for ROS 2 Lyrical and Ubuntu 24.04, new Isaac Skills for setup and manipulation, a FoundationStereo fine-tuning skill, an agent-ready inference library for the FoundationPose object pose estimation and tracking model, and a standalone pick-and-place perception skill. The item discloses no revenue, pricing, orders or customer commitments tied to the release.\ne56 NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue up 117% to $89 billion, according to the article.\ne57 NVIDIA management guided fiscal third-quarter revenue to approximately $108 billion, which the article says implies 89% growth.\ne58 NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang has projected that the company's chip sales could double in calendar year 2027.\ne59 NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, a figure the article says far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled.\ne60 The article reports that NVIDIA is financing a growing share of its sales to AI startups, with roughly 25% of fiscal 2028 revenue expected to come from customers receiving some form of company-backed financing — potentially $175 billion funded off NVIDIA's own balance sheet.\ne61 The article states that NVIDIA has off-balance-sheet guarantees exceeding $100 billion tied to projects such as the SB Energy campus for OpenAI, which it says introduces credit risk that traditional valuation metrics do not capture.\ne62 The article reports that analysts' consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA has been revised sharply higher, from $8.50 to $15.68 per share for fiscal 2029, over just the past nine months.\ne63 Singapore-founded consumer-internet group Sea said it will adopt NVIDIA's Vera Rubin computing platform to build and deploy AI models and agents at greater scale across its Shopee, Monee and Garena businesses, saying it will use Vera Rubin to extend AI work already under way there; the item gives no deployment timing, capacity, volumes or contract value.\ne64 Sea's e-commerce arm Shopee runs Compass, an in-house AI model built and run on NVIDIA graphics processors and software, which powers search, product recommendations, fraud checks and customer service; the item reports that over eight months Compass's monthly processing volume rose from 3 billion to 340 billion tokens, that it now accounts for most of Shopee's AI traffic, and that it made fraud detection 50 times more efficient than manual review and cut processing costs by 90%.\ne65 System builder CyberPowerPC is now shipping prebuilt gaming PCs equipped with NVIDIA's own GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition graphics cards (RTX 5070 or RTX 5080 Founders Edition), sold through Walmart as part of the retailer's GeForce Week promotion running 21–27 September 2026; the article notes Founders Edition cards are normally associated with NVIDIA's own retail channel and selected retailers while prebuilt systems commonly use board-partner cards, so these systems give buyers another route to NVIDIA's own RTX 5070/5080 design without purchasing the card separately. Four CyberPowerPC configurations carried the Founders Edition cards in Walmart listings.\ne66 According to the article's author, the $2,299 CyberPowerPC system pairing an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 Founders Edition with a Ryzen 7 9800X3D and 32GB DDR5-6000 memory (Walmart listing SLC8500WST) sold out in one day with over 1,000 orders; the author reads this as consistent with how much RTX 5080 cards currently cost. The unit count is the author's report of the retailer listing, not an NVIDIA disclosure.\ne67 CyberPowerPC listed prebuilt gaming PCs equipped with NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 and RTX 5070 Founders Edition GPUs on Walmart as part of the retailer's NVIDIA GeForce promotion this week; the RTX 5080 configurations ($2,299 with a Ryzen 9800X3D and $2,399 with an Intel Core Ultra 9 285K) sold out within about a day, with Walmart reportedly moving over 1,000 units, while the two RTX 5070 systems ($1,599 with a Ryzen 7800X3D and $1,549 with an Intel 14700KF) remained in stock.\ne68 TweakTown reported that third-party NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 graphics cards were selling for around $850 in the US, up from around $650 a couple of months earlier, with GPU pricing worsening because of a memory (RAM) shortage; it said standalone third-party RTX 5080 cards now start at about $1,500 in the US.\ne69 NVIDIA validation engineer Sakeena Fiza, writing in an NVIDIA corporate blog post, said she saw the NVIDIA Rubin GPU working at system level for the first time in the company's data center systems engineering lab, the first time a Rubin GPU has enumerated at system level; she describes validation as work done on a device before mass production begins and before customers depend on it. The item gives no date for the milestone, no quantities, no shipment or production timing and no customer or revenue detail.\ne70 At Nvidia AI Day Singapore, Sea Group senior director of partnerships and strategy Li Kuangli said Sea Group will be the first enterprise in Southeast Asia to adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform (Nvidia's Vera CPU combined with Rubin GPUs), as part of an AI strategy in which Sea runs every layer of its technology stack except the chips. The companies said Vera Rubin will allow Sea to build and deploy AI models and agents at a larger scale, but did not say how large the deployment will be or when it will go live.\ne71 Sea Group senior director of partnerships and strategy Li Kuangli disclosed that Sea runs its own datacentre infrastructure of over 150,000 servers and more than 25,000 GPUs across 40-plus datacentres worldwide, with a combined critical IT load in excess of 100MW; the network has more than 120 interconnections with tier-one internet service providers and handles over 1.1 exabytes of traffic a month (about 700 million hours of high-definition video, by Li's calculation).\ne72 William Tjhi, head of applied research at AI Singapore (AISG), said AISG — creator of the Sea-Lion family of open models for Southeast Asian languages — is expanding Sea-Lion with Nvidia's Nemotron open models and NeMo tools.\ne73 Nvidia vice-president of solutions architecture and engineering Marc Hamilton, speaking at Nvidia AI Day Singapore, showed GitHub data in which new repositories had climbed to 20 million a month by April, which he attributed to growing use of coding agents; he said such agents can run thousands of inferences on a single task and that some AI-native companies burnt through their annual coding budgets in the first month or two of this year.\ne74 NVIDIA announced on its developer blog the open release of NV-Reason-CT, a vision-language model purpose-built for 3D CT analysis that combines a full 3D vision transformer encoder with a Qwen3.5-4B language model to generate radiologist-style chain-of-thought reasoning and structured reports; NVIDIA says the model is now openly available for research and development, with weights on Hugging Face and code on GitHub. NVIDIA describes it as an open research and development foundation, not an autonomous diagnostic system or a cleared clinical product, and reports state-of-the-art CT-RATE benchmark results (Macro-F1 0.614, Macro-AUROC 0.871) versus published 3D contrastive and fused 2D/3D baselines. No revenue, pricing, customer order or capacity commitment is attached to the release.\ne75 IonQ announced on 23 September 2026 that it will make the first on-premise quantum computing deployment at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC): an IonQ Superion 256 system will be installed at the facility and directly linked to an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 system via NVIDIA NVQLink, with workloads orchestrated by the open NVIDIA CUDA-Q platform, under a joint research program on hybrid software development and large-scale system prototyping. IonQ said installation at NVAQC is scheduled for next year (2027).\ne76 Nvidia told shareholders in May 2026 that it would raise its quarterly dividend to $0.25 per share from $0.01 per share, an increase the Morningstar author calculates at 2,400%. The author estimates roughly $25 billion per year would be returned to shareholders through the dividend, which would make Nvidia one of the largest dividend payers in the US market; that annual figure is the author's approximation, not a company-disclosed total.\ne77 Nvidia announced an $80 billion share buyback program at the time of its May 2026 dividend declaration, per the Morningstar article.\ne78 Morningstar, recapping the year's Nvidia news in September 2026, refers to Nvidia's forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth, without stating the period or scope those forecasts cover. The article gives the forecast as context for how Nvidia's valuation and growth profile sit against its dividend.\ne79 Morningstar, listing the year's major Nvidia news in September 2026, describes Nvidia's \"role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments\" as one of the threads around which its dividend announcement was overlooked. The article does not specify the form of that financing (equity, debt, credit support or guarantees), the counterparties, or the period covered.\ne80 The Trump administration has allowed Nvidia to ship its H200 AI chips to approved customers in China, per the article; the H200 is described as an older-generation product behind Nvidia's current Blackwell chips.\ne81 Chinese authorities have so far restricted shipments of Nvidia's H200 chips into China, according to the article, despite U.S. permission for those shipments to approved customers.\ne82 Nvidia has not factored any sales from China into its outlook for the year, according to the article — meaning any resumption of China shipments would be incremental to its stated outlook.\ne83 NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter 2027 consolidated revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, with Data Center segment revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, and non-GAAP gross margin of 75% versus 72.5% a year earlier, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release as cited by Zacks.\ne84 NVIDIA guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, which at the midpoint would represent a 12% sequential increase, as cited by Zacks.\ne85 NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform has entered the full production stage, positioning the company to benefit from the next phase of AI infrastructure investment, as reported by Zacks.\ne86 NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang is scheduled to attend President Donald Trump's state dinner for Chinese President Xi Jinping on Sept. 24, 2026, along with other technology leaders, as the U.S. and China discuss AI, trade, tariffs and advanced semiconductors. The article says the dinner itself does not guarantee policy changes but could provide a backdrop for signals on NVIDIA's access to the Chinese market and export restrictions.\ne87 NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, 2026, for the quarter ended July 26: revenue rose 106% year over year to a record $96.2 billion (up 18% sequentially) and exceeded prior guidance of $91 billion plus or minus 2%. Non-GAAP net income rose 118% to $54 billion, adjusted EPS rose 120% to $2.22, non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%, and operating income rose 124% to $63.7 billion. Data Center revenue was $89 billion, up 117% year over year and the majority of total revenue.\ne88 NVIDIA guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, and GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins to approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points. The forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China.\ne89 Nebius Group announced another increase in prices for NVIDIA GPU rentals, and CoreWeave said it was continuing to contract new compute capacity at higher prices; the article cites both as fresh evidence that demand for NVIDIA-powered computing remains strong. No price levels, capacity amounts or dates are given.\ne90 NVIDIA management pointed to full production of its next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform, and the article says continued AI infrastructure strength is accelerating NVIDIA's AI growth trajectory. The statement does not say Vera Rubin has begun volume customer shipments or revenue recognition.\ne91 Street analysts expect NVIDIA's EPS to grow 102.4% year over year to $9.25 in fiscal 2027, followed by another 65.7% increase to $15.33 in fiscal 2028, according to the article's consensus forecast.\ne92 AI cloud provider Nscale filed for a U.S. initial public offering on 18 September 2026 disclosing that it lost $1.02 billion in the first six months of 2026 on revenue of just $140.6 million — the financial condition of the counterparty to which NVIDIA is committing $1 billion of convertible financing.\ne93 NVIDIA is committing $1 billion to a $3.1 billion convertible financing for AI cloud provider Nscale, the IPO candidate whose filing the article discusses; the article notes this gives NVIDIA direct capital exposure in addition to its role as hardware supplier.\ne94 Nscale disclosed that as of 31 August 2026 it had $103.4 billion of active and contracted total contract value under long-term take-or-pay contracts with a weighted-average contract life of about 5.7 years, operating in 14 regions with more than 10 gigawatts of potential power capacity — the contracted demand base underlying the Nscale build-out NVIDIA supplies and is financing.\ne95 Nscale disclosed that a single customer generated 52% of its first-half 2026 revenue, and its future plan leans heavily on Microsoft and Anthropic, indicating concentrated demand behind its contract book.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"statement\":\"e1\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e2\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e3\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e4\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e5\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e6\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e7\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e8\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e9\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Sea's adoption makes yes more likely: a named customer plans to use Vera Rubin, although shipment timing and volume are unspecified.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e10\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e11\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e12\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e13\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e14\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e15\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e16\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e17\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e18\",\"v1\":\"NVIDIA expects substantial business from labs it backs, making larger support commitments more plausible, though the figure does not identify guarantees or their amounts.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e19\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e20\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e21\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e22\",\"v1\":\"Planned credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts is a named component of the total, making a higher disclosed amount more likely; no dollar value is given.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e23\",\"v1\":\"Minimum-revenue guarantees for some cloud capacity are part of the requested total, making a higher disclosure more likely; their value is unspecified.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e24\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e25\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e26\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e27\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e28\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e29\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e30\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e31\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e32\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e33\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e34\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e35\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e36\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e37\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e38\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e39\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e40\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e41\",\"v1\":\"Credit support for 4.25 gigawatts, with an option for 3.75 more, makes a larger total more likely, although the statement gives no dollar amount.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e42\",\"v1\":\"Disclosed maximum guarantee exposure of $105 billion under conditions makes the $100 billion-or-more answer more plausible; the maximum is not necessarily the reportable total.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e43\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e44\",\"v1\":\"The report says customer credit support and long-dated guarantees are increasing, making higher disclosed commitments more likely, without quantifying them.\",\"v2\":\"The report says supply commitments are increasing, making higher purchase-obligation brackets more likely, although it provides no amount.\",\"v3\":\"China remains largely closed to data-center compute, making permission for Blackwell shipments less likely than if the market were already open.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e45\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e46\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e47\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e48\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e49\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e50\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e51\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e52\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e53\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e54\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e55\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e56\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e57\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e58\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e59\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e60\",\"v1\":\"Extensive NVIDIA-backed customer financing makes larger support commitments plausible, but the $175 billion estimate is not itself a guarantee total.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e61\",\"v1\":\"Reported guarantees exceeding $100 billion make the highest bracket more likely, subject to their scope and inclusion in the requested disclosures.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e62\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e63\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Sea plans to adopt Vera Rubin, making yes more likely through customer demand, but gives no shipment date or volume.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e64\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e65\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e66\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e67\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e68\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e69\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"A Rubin GPU worked at system level in validation, making eventual shipments more plausible, though the undated milestone does not establish volume or timing.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e70\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Sea plans to adopt Vera Rubin, making yes more likely through customer demand; deployment timing and size remain unspecified.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e71\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e72\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e73\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e74\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e75\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e76\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e77\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e78\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e79\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e80\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"U.S. approval for older H200 exports shows willingness to permit some NVIDIA AI chips, modestly favoring yes, though Blackwell is more advanced.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e81\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"China's restrictions on the older H200 make yes less likely: Chinese permission is also needed for the newer Blackwell shipments.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e82\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"NVIDIA's outlook assumes no China sales this year, making near-term resumption less likely; it does not establish the January outcome.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e83\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e84\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e85\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Full production makes yes more likely because the platform has progressed toward volume shipments, though shipments and revenue recognition are not established.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e86\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e87\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e88\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"The next-quarter forecast assumes no China data-center compute revenue, making an immediate reopening less likely, though it does not settle January's outcome.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e89\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e90\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Management's report of full production makes yes more likely by placing Vera Rubin closer to volume shipment; it does not establish shipment or recognized revenue.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e91\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e92\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e93\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e94\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e95\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}"}}
